            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for to stir up, then the Urdu for the public."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: انکار کرنا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "انکار کرنا — inkār karnā — \"to deny; to refuse\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اس نے چوری سے انکار کیا۔ us ne chorī se inkār kiyā. He denied the theft."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with نے (he or she …): اس نے انکار کیا, us ne inkār kiyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "انکار کرنا (inkār karnā) is built from inkār, usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic inkār, \"a denial\", and کرنا. What is denied takes سے: چوری سے انکار کیا."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
